id: questions/what-is-this
title: "What is this?"
kind: orientation-question
status: preview
updated: 2026-07-11

short_answer: >
  .yawn is a plain-text shape for making orientation, inference, missing
  information, boundaries, movement, proof, and memory visible before action.

why_it_exists: >
  Humans and AI systems both act from partial models. .yawn gives them a shared
  object where observations and inferences can be inspected without turning
  either one into hidden authority.

relationship:
  yawn_file: "the portable orientation and memory shape"
  yawn_bot: "the official co-orientation runtime that loads the shape across wallet, browser, office, object, and world projections"
  yawn_ai: "the intelligence substrate behind those interfaces"

public_boundary: >
  This repository contains portable protocol contracts, examples, and
  conformance evidence. Private memory, credentials, private runtime state, and
  proprietary implementation do not belong here.

smallest_loop:
  - notice
  - orient
  - infer
  - name what is missing
  - protect the boundary
  - choose or defer a move
  - prove what changed
  - replay

read_next:
  - questions/where-am-i.yawn
  - start/first-yawn.yawn
  - examples/stuck.yawn

boundary:
  - "This does not claim reality is literally code."
  - "Signal is not instruction."
  - "AI output is not authority."
